    "title": "$R(D^*)$, $|V_{cb}|$, and the Heavy Quark Symmetry relations between form factors",
    "abstract": "Stringent relations between the $B^{(*)} \\to D^{(*)} $ form factors exist in the heavy quark limit and the leading symmetry breaking corrections are known. We reconsider their uncertainty and role in the analysis of recent Belle data for $B\\to D^{(*)}\\ell\\nu$ with model-independent parametrizations and in the related prediction of $R(D^{(*)})$. We find $|V_{cb}|=41.5(1.3) \\ 10^{-3}$ and $|V_{cb}|=40.6(^{+1.2}_{-1.3}) \\ 10^{-3}$ using input from Light Cone Sum Rules, and $R(D^{*})=0.260(8)$.",
